---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/Briefing.css';
---

<Layout title="ORION // OP 2: The Quiet Line - Briefing" description="Field briefing for Operation The Quiet Line - Korpiharju ridge, Zone-21 Finland." nav={[{ href: '/orion-fimbulwinter/mission-control/', label: '<- MISSION CONTROL' }, { href: '#situation', label: 'SITUATION' }, { href: '#mission', label: 'MISSION' }, { href: '#ground', label: 'GROUND' }, { href: '#execution', label: 'EXECUTION' }, { href: '#roe', label: 'ROE' }, { href: '#support', label: 'SUPPORT' }]} footer="ORION INTERNATIONAL - ZONE-21 // FIMBULWINTER - OP 2: THE QUIET LINE - BRIEFING" decryptLines={['ORION SECURE UPLINK - CHANNEL 21', 'AUTHENTICATING OPERATOR...', 'CLEARANCE CONFIRMED - FIELD COMMAND', 'DECRYPTING DOSSIER: OPERATION THE QUIET LINE']}>
  <div class="briefing-actions"><button class="print-opord" type="button">PRINT OPORD</button></div>
  <section id="situation" class="briefing-section"><h1 class="op-name">SITUATION</h1><h2 class="op-title">OPERATION THE QUIET LINE</h2><div class="reveal"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Four days after Signal Fire, the 44th Army Corps' main body is across the border and moving past Ahola toward the next FDF line. The village is behind them now. Whatever got out, got out.</p><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The corps runs this whole sector on wire and short-hop UHF - no satellite links worth intercepting, no drones. Every tasking, every fire request, every supply movement passes through a handful of ground relay nodes, and the hardened one for this sector sits on the forest ridge northwest of Ahola that the locals call Korpiharju. <span class="intel-source">[SOURCE: ORION SIGINT - RELIABILITY A-2]</span></p><aside class="margin-note note-a">sit at the desk, don't break it</aside></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion does not want it destroyed. An order sent from that transmitter, in the corps' own format, with current authentication, is believed up and down the sector net. Orion intends to send exactly one: a resupply request. A forward Russian unit, apparently bleeding - out of ammunition, short of weapons and men - asking corps logistics for an emergency push. The corps will answer it by rolling a convoy toward a grid Orion chose. Orion will be on the road.</p><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Two things make this a one-night job. The transmitter's authentication only works with the current key set, which the corps rotates on a fixed schedule - and the Chief of Signals, Colonel Arkady Volkov, is forward on the ridge this week running the handover in person. <span class="intel-source">[SOURCE: FDF LIAISON - RELIABILITY B-2]</span> <span class="intel-warning">WINDOW CLOSES ON ROTATION - FIELD VERIFICATION REQUIRED</span></p><aside class="margin-note note-b">the colonel and the keys, same night</aside></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Chernov wants tempo. A forward unit screaming for ammunition is exactly the kind of thing he clears fast, because a stalled sub-unit is a stalled advance. His impatience is what makes the bait work.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A freelance journalist, Nieminen, is still working the region. Orion is still not here officially.</p></div></section>
  <section id="mission" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">MISSION</h2><h3 class="op-title">TASKING</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">FIELD COMMAND DIRECTIVE</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion elements will intercept Colonel Volkov and recover the 44th's current sector key set intact; assault and hold the Korpiharju communications hub long enough to seize its transmitter and signals log intact; transmit one authenticated resupply request over the corps net to draw a Russian resupply convoy onto a route of Orion's choosing; and ambush that convoy, stripping or destroying its load before the corps QRF can react.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">On completion Orion will conduct a fighting withdrawal west off the ridge.</p></div></section>
  <section id="ground"><h2 class="op-name">GROUND</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD NAVIGATION</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">TERRAIN // KORPIHARJU SECTOR</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A forest road and a corps forward CP northeast of the ridge (Phase 1). The fortified comms hub on the Korpiharju high ground itself (Phase 2). A stretch of the convoy's route - a forested defile where the road narrows, with a level crossing - west of the ridge for the ambush and the break west (Phase 4).</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12px;">Tactical overlay to follow once Eden placement is locked. Phase positions above are directional, not gridded.</p></div></section>
  <section id="execution" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">EXECUTION</h2><h3 class="op-title">ORDER OF BATTLE</h3><div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-1" data-phase="1"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="1" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 1 / 4</div><h3>Take the Keys</h3><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Intercept Colonel Volkov as he moves between the corps forward CP and the ridge with a small security detail. Recover the fill device and codebook intact - damaged key material fails the operation's purpose. Keep it quiet: if the corps registers him lost or the keys compromised before Phase 3, they rotate early and the transmission is worthless. Ground element chooses the ambush on the move or a hit on the forward CP.</p><aside class="margin-note note-c">no rounds through the pack</aside></div></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-2" data-phase="2"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="2" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 2 / 4</div><h3>Take the Hub</h3><div class="annotated"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Establish an OP, then breach the perimeter and clear the position. The loud part of the night. Cut the buried landline trunk on the way in - radio only from here. The transmitter and encryption set are NOT to be demolished; Orion needs them working. Pull the signals log: current call-signs, authentication tables, unit designations, and the logistics reporting format. Hold the position.</p><aside class="margin-note note-d">the box stays intact</aside></div></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-3" data-phase="3"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="3" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 3 / 4</div><h3>The False Request</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">With Volkov's keys and the log's authentication, send one keyed resupply request in the corps' own format - a named forward unit reporting heavy losses, out of ammunition, needing replacement weapons and personnel, requesting an emergency push to a grid Orion specifies. How the request is framed is the operation's fixed decision, and it colours the Russian opening in the finale:</p><ul class="reveal decrypt-scroll"><li><strong>Frontline unit combat-ineffective</strong> - the corps shoves its reserve forward to hold the line.</li><li><strong>Rear echelon hit on the supply route</strong> - the corps peels security back to guard its own rear.</li><li><strong>Unit needs full relief, not resupply</strong> - the corps rotates a fresh formation in.</li></ul></div><div class="phase climax reveal" id="execution-phase-4" data-phase="4"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="4" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 4 / 4</div><h3>Spring the Ambush</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Move ahead of the convoy to the killzone on its route - a forested defile where the road narrows. Set the blocking position, mines, and support-by-fire; let the escort commit, then hit it. Break the escort, take what can be carried off the trucks - ammunition, weapons, medical - and destroy the rest on site; the load is the point, do not burn it all down reflexively.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A convoy going silent in the wrong place brings the corps QRF, and - if the hub was left manned - its garrison, down on the route. Once the trucks are dealt with, break contact west off the ridge with the load, giving ground deliberately rather than holding a fixed line. Decision at the level crossing: blow the captured transmitter now - clean break, the loss registers instantly, the deception has hours - or leave it standing and keyed, and it keeps propagating while a real corps transmission may get through and contradict it.</p></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim); font-size:12px;">Ground commanders retain discretionary authority over internal task allocation and approach across all phases.</p></div></section>
  <section id="roe" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">RULES OF ENGAGEMENT</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD RESTRICTIONS</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">ROE // EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY</div><div class="annotated"><ul class="reveal decrypt-scroll"><li>Any 44th Army Corps element observed, in contact, or confirmed at a designated objective or on the convoy is hostile.</li><li>Colonel Volkov is a capture-or-kill HVT. The key set matters more than the man - do not let a firefight put rounds through the fill device or burn the codebook.</li><li>The transmitter, encryption set, and signals log at the hub are mission-critical and are not to be destroyed before Phase 3 is complete.</li><li>The convoy load is a recovery objective, not just a target. Strip what is useful before destroying the remainder.</li><li>Lethal force is authorised against confirmed hostile positions without further clearance. This is a direct-action and ambush operation, not a restrained security posture.</li><li>A journalist, Nieminen - freelance, persistent - is working the region. Orion is not officially present. Do not get photographed.</li><li>Self-defence is authorised at all times without prior command approval.</li></ul><aside class="margin-note note-e">copy that</aside></div></div></section>
  <section id="support" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">SUPPORT</h2><h3 class="op-title">AVAILABLE ASSETS</h3><div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">COMMS</div><h3>Recovered In-Mission</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The FDF listening post at the treeline hands over the initial fix on Volkov's movement and the hub layout, then goes quiet - it will not acknowledge Orion on any net. Sector frequencies and the hub's authentication are not held at start; they are recovered in Phase 1 (keys) and Phase 2 (log).</p></div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">AIR SUPPORT</div><h3>Valkyrie</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Valkyrie provides limited CAS and overwatch in this sector on request through mission command. No standing air presence. No dedicated extraction airframe is assigned - plan the egress on the ground.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="operator-note" class="operator-note reveal" aria-label="Operator's note"><div class="head">OFF-RECORD // FOR THE PERSON WHO READS TO THE END</div><p>You are going to fight your way into a hub, sit at someone else's desk, and ask their army to send you a truck full of ammunition. Then you are going to take it off them in the trees.</p><p>Send the request once. Be on the road before it arrives. Be a long way west before anyone works out no such unit ever called.</p></section>
  <script>
    const unlockPhase = (phase: string) => {
      const blip = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(`.blip[data-phase="${phase}"]`);
      if (!blip) return;
      blip.classList.remove('locked');
      blip.removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
      blip.removeAttribute('tabindex');
    };
    document.querySelectorAll('.blip').forEach((blip) => blip.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const target = document.querySelector(blip.dataset.target || '');
      if (!(target instanceof HTMLElement) || blip.classList.contains('locked')) return;
      const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reducedMotion ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      target.classList.remove('flash');
      void target.offsetWidth;
      target.classList.add('flash');
      window.setTimeout(() => target.classList.remove('flash'), 1500);
    }));
    const phaseObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (!entry.isIntersecting || !(entry.target instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
        const phase = entry.target.dataset.phase;
        if (!phase) return;
        unlockPhase(phase);
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.45 });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.phase[data-phase]').forEach((phase) => phaseObserver.observe(phase));

    const checklistKey = 'orion-checklist-op2';
    const completePhases = new Set<number>(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(checklistKey) || '[]'));
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-checklist-phase]').forEach((input) => {
      const phase = Number(input.dataset.checklistPhase);
      input.checked = completePhases.has(phase);
      input.addEventListener('change', () => {
        input.checked ? completePhases.add(phase) : completePhases.delete(phase);
        localStorage.setItem(checklistKey, JSON.stringify([...completePhases]));
      });
    });

    document.querySelector('.print-opord')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
  </script>
</Layout>
